Okay, here's how I approached this. First, I broke down the request: travel in Minangkabau, at least three sentences, and more than 25 words. Next, I formulated the content. I envisioned a trip to West Sumatra, focusing on Bukittinggi and Harau Valley, and, of course, the food. I then drafted the sentences in Minangkabau. The first sentence is "Bajalan-jalan ka ranah Minang ko sabana manyanangkan ati, karano banyak tampek rancak nan sasuai untuak malapeh panek," (Traveling to the Minang land is truly pleasing to the heart, because there are many beautiful places suitable for releasing tiredness.) After that I wrote "Kito bisa pai malala ka Bukittinggi untuak malihat Jam Gadang, atau singgah ka Lambah Harau nan dikuliliangi dek bukik batu nan tinggi mambana." (We can go wandering to Bukittinggi to see the Jam Gadang, or stop by Harau Valley which is surrounded by very high stone hills.) The last sentence is "Salain pamandangan nan elok, di sapanjang jalan kito juo bisa mancubo bagai-bagai kuliner nan lamak rasonyo, cando randang jo sate padang." (Besides the beautiful scenery, along the way we can also try various delicious culinary delights, like rendang and sate padang.) Finally, I reviewed the grammar, corrected a couple of phrases ("malapeh panek" and "nan dikuliliangi"), and made sure the sentence and word counts were met.


